  * A root sits on the unit circle -- an MA root (modulus 0.99995).  The
    likelihood rose towards a non-invertible MA and the optimiser stopped
    at the engine's invertibility gate: this is a CONSTRAINED point, not an
    interior maximum.  The standard errors of the MA are not defined along
    that direction, and no LR that uses this fit has its usual
    distribution (BUG-49).
    The combination the model differences once too often -- the left
    null vector u of Theta*(1), smallest singular value 4.98e-05 -- has
    weights (|u|, on Ybar = [nabla Y2 ; W]):
